WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:04.900
<b>Hakone</b>

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:08.400
<b>Tokyo-Hakone Round-Trip College Ekiden Race</b>

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:07.910
The time is 7:59.

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:13.200
The Tokyo-Hakone Round-Trip
College Ekiden Race will begin shortly.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.780
<b>Hakone Ekiden</b>

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:13.200
<b>Tokyo-Hakone Round-Trip College Ekiden Race</b>

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:18.430
Which university will write
a new page in history?

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.910
<b>Kansei University</b>

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:24.020
Twenty-one runners wearing sashes
will wrap themselves in a gust of wind

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.740
as they run down Hakoneji Road.

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:30.420
Will that wind be a headwind or a tailwind?

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.880
Tokyo-Hakone Round-Trip College Ekiden Race

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:34.260
Who will be the first to return to Otemachi?

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:38.780
They are starting now towards honor and glory!

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:53.990
<b><i>Run with the Wind</i></b>

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:23.410
<b>Section 1</b>

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:15.740
The Tokyo-Hakone Round-Trip
College Ekiden Race

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:18.400
allows no room for carelessness
once again this year.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.870
The runners have maintained
a slow pace since the start of the race.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:25.800
They're averaging 3:07 per kilometer
over the first three kilometers.

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:31.920
Broadcast Car

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:30.500
For the past few years, we'd been seeing
high-paced starts under three minutes.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:31.920
What do you think of this?

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:37.590
<b>New Year Sports Special <b>Hakone Ekiden</b></b>

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:35.770
Everyone's looking for their opportunity.

00:02:35.770 --> 00:02:37.590
They rival each other in ability.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:41.300
<b>Section 1</b>

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:41.300
More than speed, they must
be emphasizing strategy.

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:47.640
Come on.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:50.600
Run where we can see you, Prince.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:53.150
Wait! He might be doing it on purpose.

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:55.900
A windbreak?

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:57.670
That's right.

00:02:57.670 --> 00:02:59.730
Each section of the Hakone Ekiden is long.

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:01.530
The situation changes moment to moment.

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:05.010
To ensure you don't fall
behind during the second half,

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:07.240
conserve your stamina during the first.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.830
Use everything you can.

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:12.060
Conserve my stamina, huh?

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:14.710
I hope I'm allowed to do that.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.800
You will. I'm sure you will.

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:23.800
<i>What is he? A prophet?</i>

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:26.680
How is he doing?

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:27.960
<i>He's doing well.</i>

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:29.640
<i>He's coming up on ten kilometers.</i>

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:32.380
It's a truly dry affair.

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:34.560
This is no different than going for a drive.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:35.710
<i>Got it.</i>

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:38.140
<i>If you see any change in Prince,</i>

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:40.320
Yamanote

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:40.320
could you offer him words of encouragement?

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:43.700
Tell him...

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:48.790
<b><i>The Moment of Release</i></b>

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:57.380
Kashiwazaki!

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.580
This kilometer's exactly three minutes!

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:01.170
Keep your pace!

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:11.600
<b>Rokugo Bridge</b>

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:12.280
<i>The runners have made it 17 kilometers now.</i>

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:14.980
<i>The incline of Rokugo
Bridge lies in their path.</i>

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:19.120
<i>If they exhaust themselves here,
they'll pay for it later.</i>

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:20.940
<i>They'll have to stand firm.</i>

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:29.620
<i>They're moving! The runners are on the move!</i>

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.750
<i>The quiet journey so far is being
disrupted by major change!</i>

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:37.230
<i>Yokohama, Eurasia, Teito, and other
universities are increasing their paces!</i>

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.240
<i>But I don't like inclines.</i>

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:59.060
Even if the runners around
you begin to move, don't panic.

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:03.030
Just keeping up with them until Rokugo
Bridge earns full marks from me.

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:08.070
You'll be able to pass the sash to Musa
without much of a difference in time.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:11.490
I see. The real race is Section 2 and onward.

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:13.120
Are you unhappy with that?

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:16.460
Not at all. I'm only an amateur.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:20.880
I'll finish the race quickly, so I
can get back to my comics sooner.

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:22.750
That's all.

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:29.450
Things might have gotten a little easier.

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:30.810
Prince.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:35.520
Sorry for forcing you to do this.

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:49.540
<i>If I give up, the race is over.</i>

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:55.120
<i>All those who succeed have worked hard.</i>

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:58.250
<i>I am strong!</i>

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:12.600
<b>Tsurumi Relay Station</b>

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:10.950
The air at Tsurumi Relay
Station is heating up

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:13.040
as the sashes will be arriving soon.

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:16.450
This year's Section 2 will be a fierce race

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:19.750
featuring athletes running
10,000 meters in 28 minutes.

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:22.650
And we can't discuss Section 2
without mentioning this man:

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:25.480
Iwanki of Kofu Academy.

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:30.620
<i>We're all very excited to see how
he'll run in his fourth Hakone Ekiden.</i>

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:36.120
<i>We'll also be watching Kansei
University's exchange student, Musa.</i>

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:40.080
Musa is a truly unique runner.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.640
He's a government-sponsored
engineering student,

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:46.330
who had no running
experience until last spring.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:49.170
Thank you.

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:51.850
Kansei University is taking on the
Hakone Ekiden with only ten runners,

00:06:51.850 --> 00:06:54.280
and each runner is exceptionally unique.

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:03.440
I enjoyed the qualifier.

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:05.980
I'm disappointed we won't get to race again.

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:08.690
Don't worry.

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:10.470
He won't let you take it easy.

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:11.660
Not our ace.

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:28.210
Hey, Musa.

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:30.760
I just saw you on TV.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:32.300
<i>I was surprised.</i>

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:34.480
<i>Did I look weird?</i>

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:35.600
Not at all.

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:40.460
Musa, once this is over, let's go see the snow.

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:42.050
Snow?

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:45.480
<i>Yeah. It really snows in my hometown.</i>

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:48.650
<i>The world becomes white
as far as the eye can see.</i>

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.000
<i>You've never seen that, have you?</i>

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:51.580
I haven't.

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:56.600
<i>I'll imagine us having
a snowball fight while I run.</i>

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:58.360
Sounds nice.

00:07:58.360 --> 00:07:59.710
<i>Talk to you later.</i>

00:07:59.710 --> 00:08:00.670
Later.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:09.760
You can't afford to be worrying
about the others.

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:22.480
Section 1 20km Point

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:35.240
Prince!

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:37.620
Message for you from Haiji!

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:40.990
“There's something I never got to tell you!”

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:46.010
“Come to Tsurumi even if
you have to crawl!” That's all!

00:08:49.810 --> 00:08:52.620
That's not what I want to hear.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:57.390
Joe and Hanamichi, Ippo and Sakamichi.

00:08:57.390 --> 00:09:00.210
Sango Jugo, Hinata, and Yawara.

00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:04.230
Sena, Goro, Tsubasa, Ryoma.

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:06.700
It's no use. There's no end to them.

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:14.030
I like protagonists, but I also
like the people who lead them.

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:18.090
They're all tough, but of course they are.

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:20.660
They don't want to be shown kindness.

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:24.960
An athlete wants to win.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:38.930
Totai Uni is the 16th to pass their sash.

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:41.460
They're 40 seconds behind first place.

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:42.010
Kansei University!

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:43.970
Behind them are Nihonbashi
Tech and Jonan Bunka.

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:45.310
Kansei University to the relay line!

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:55.420
<i>I hate this.</i>

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:59.670
<i>I really hate running.</i>

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:03.290
<i>I got dragged into this</i>

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:06.450
<i>and suffered for it.</i>

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:12.340
<i>But if I hadn't run with them...</i>

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:15.960
<i>If I hadn't made it here...</i>

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:19.470
<i>I...</i>

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:22.720
<i>I would've hated myself more!</i>

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:30.490
Prince!

00:10:32.450 --> 00:10:35.940
Prince! I'm here!

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:38.900
Prince!

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:46.620
<i>There's someone waiting for me there.</i>

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:52.500
<i>Just thinking about it makes me so... so...</i>

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:54.800
<i>I...</i>

00:10:59.230 --> 00:10:59.800
Prince!

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:03.220
I take back what I said.

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:05.680
Prince.

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:07.930
Thank you.

00:11:08.170 --> 00:11:10.360
Non-participants, stay off the course!

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:14.540
I pass.

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:19.850
Yes!

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:21.070
Nice!

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:24.320
Yeah!

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:29.040
<b>Section 2</b>

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:38.170
<i>The pace sudden quickened
as soon as we entered Section 2.</i>

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:41.130
<i>I have to keep up.</i>

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:45.510
<i>Prince got the sash this far.</i>

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:48.050
<i>I promise I'll take it to Totsuka.</i>

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:58.180
<i>Wow...</i>

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:04.610
I told him! I know I did!

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:09.510
I told him to restrain himself
around the five-kilometer mark!

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:11.870
<b>Yokohama Station</b>

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:12.470
Maybe Musa didn't hear me.

00:12:12.470 --> 00:12:14.840
Tell him again at ten kilometers.

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:16.030
He's going too fast.

00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:17.090
Got it.

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:21.020
He's averaging 2:48 per kilometer.

00:12:21.020 --> 00:12:22.920
He won't last until the end.

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:24.900
He got carried away.

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:30.020
<b>Gontazaka</b>

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:45.320
<i>Why can't I catch up?</i>

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:47.640
<i>My legs won't move.</i>

00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:48.890
<i>They won't move.</i>

00:12:48.890 --> 00:12:51.830
Musa! Musa! Musa!

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:54.660
You're 18th right now.

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:57.630
There's a cluster of seven up ahead.

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:04.220
People build it up by calling it the
Glorious Section 2, the section of aces,

00:13:04.900 --> 00:13:06.970
but don't listen to them.

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:10.100
Plenty of schools think 
other sections decide the race.

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:12.800
Let's think of Section 2's 23 kilometers

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:16.460
as one part of a longer race
the ten of us build together.

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:17.310
Okay.

00:13:18.050 --> 00:13:20.270
Bravely, calmly, and without fail.

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:22.960
Only you can do it.

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:30.360
<i>18th. In other words, 
even I could pass two runners.</i>

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:36.290
<i>Bravely, calmly, and without fail.</i>

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:37.800
<i>This is Broadcast Car 2.</i>

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:50.510
<b>Section 2</b>

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:39.640
<i>Iwanki's pace remains constant.</i>

00:13:39.640 --> 00:13:42.240
<i>Perhaps he exhausted himself
competing against Manaka's Inawa,</i>

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:44.120
<i>who caught up to Rikudo to reach first place,</i>

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:46.520
<i>but he can't catch Tokyo Sport.</i>

00:13:46.520 --> 00:13:48.700
<i>The burst of speed
at the start of the section</i>

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:51.910
<i>is throwing off even the strongest athletes.</i>

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:54.180
Why aren't they showing Musa?

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:57.350
It can't be helped. 
The race for first is crazy.

00:13:57.350 --> 00:14:00.280
Yeah, but don't you wanna see him?

00:13:57.350 --> 00:14:04.030
<b>1 Manaka
2 Rikudo
3 Boso
4 Tokyo Sport
5 Kofu Academy
6 Yokohama
7 Kino
8 Shinsei
9 Kanagawa
10 Nihonbashi Tech
11 Eurasia
12 Do
13 Jonan Bunka
14 Tokyo Academy
15 Ake
16 Kitakan
OP Student Association
17 Kansei
18 Yamato
19 Teito
20 Saikyo</b>

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:04.280
King, how's your job hunt coming?

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:05.140
Huh?

00:14:05.140 --> 00:14:08.590
I thought I'd relieve the tension.

00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:10.690
Then choose your words more carefully.

00:14:10.690 --> 00:14:12.490
Okay...

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:17.740
I haven't been doing it.

00:14:17.740 --> 00:14:18.420
Huh?

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:20.750
When would I have had the time?

00:14:21.070 --> 00:14:22.710
What? Then what are you going to do?

00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:27.640
I don't know!

00:14:28.670 --> 00:14:31.050
What are my parents going to say?

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:33.010
Then why don't you run next year?

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:35.730
I won't be able to look for a job again!

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:37.130
You're right.

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:41.230
Next year? Are you...

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:45.940
Get ready! They're coming!

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:47.910
Oof.

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:50.410
King, wanna warm up together?

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:55.870
<b>19km Point</b>

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:01.780
<i>I thought I reduced my pace.</i>

00:15:09.190 --> 00:15:11.150
<i>Running is strange.</i>

00:15:11.150 --> 00:15:13.000
<i>Speed alone isn't enough to win.</i>

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:15.740
<i>You have opponents and teammates.</i>

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:17.050
You're almost there!

00:15:17.050 --> 00:15:18.090
You can do it!

00:15:18.090 --> 00:15:20.220
<i>Someone's voice gives you strength.</i>

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:22.630
<i>And that's how I run!</i>

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:35.280
<b>Totsuka Relay Point</b>

00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:37.990
Kofu Academy's Iwanki leaves four
years of passion on Hakoneji Road

00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:39.560
as he arrives at the relay line!

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:44.040
He failed to win his section,

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:46.540
but he displayed his usual
unchanging running style

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:48.680
in a turbulent Section 2, nonetheless.

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:00.460
Marvelous.

00:16:01.170 --> 00:16:05.030
You were extremely fortunate
to have been able to run with him.

00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:09.190
Yes. His running is the embodiment of strength.

00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:11.110
Musa!

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:22.700
Over here!

00:16:25.280 --> 00:16:26.670
Thanks, ace.

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:34.490
Musa!

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:37.390
14th. You were 14th.

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:39.900
You passed seven guys.

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:42.730
Whoa! Whoa!

00:16:43.780 --> 00:16:46.100
<i>The temperature is currently 5.7 degrees.</i>

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:51.280
<i>The sunlight and sea breeze, together,
chip away at the runners' stamina.</i>

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:54.860
<i>Musa was amazing.</i>

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:56.930
<i>It makes me want to do the same thing.</i>

00:16:57.440 --> 00:16:59.840
<i>King seems to be taking
the race seriously, too.</i>

00:16:59.840 --> 00:17:01.480
<i>We even locked eyes.</i>

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:06.040
<i>He practically told me 
he'd be running next year, too.</i>

00:17:06.820 --> 00:17:08.480
<i>Next year, huh?</i>

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:10.310
<i>Sorry, King.</i>

00:17:10.820 --> 00:17:14.630
<i>This is probably the end for me.</i>

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:29.420
<i>Joji, my younger brother, is a part of my soul.</i>

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:34.320
<i>We slept together, played together,
and went to school together.</i>

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:36.780
<i>No one could tell us apart.</i>

00:17:37.370 --> 00:17:41.240
<i>They seemed troubled when we spoke to them,</i>

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:44.330
<i>and we'd do things to distress them further.</i>

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:50.600
<i>But we're two different people.</i>

00:17:51.240 --> 00:17:54.870
<i>I'm Jo Taro. He's Jo Jiro.</i>

00:17:56.730 --> 00:17:58.990
<i>We have plenty of differences.</i>

00:17:58.990 --> 00:18:04.040
<i>Favorite foods, the locations of
our moles, the girls we've dated.</i>

00:18:04.040 --> 00:18:05.250
<i>Our personalities...</i>

00:18:06.050 --> 00:18:07.350
<i>...and our talents.</i>

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:13.310
<i>I'm sure of it. Joji's the better runner.</i>

00:18:13.310 --> 00:18:17.890
<i>Even if there's no difference now,
Joji will become way faster than me.</i>

00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:21.180
<i>He'll see worlds I can't see.</i>

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:25.120
<i>After all, you love to run.</i>

00:18:26.130 --> 00:18:29.340
<i>He'd sometimes train by himself before dawn.</i>

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:32.750
<i>How can he run like that?</i>

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:39.660
Bro, can you watch my form?

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:44.010
<i>When we were together, the conversation
would always turn to Kakeru.</i>

00:18:45.580 --> 00:18:51.340
<i>Joji, you finally found your very own rival.</i>

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:53.120
<i>Your very own goal.</i>

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:56.380
<i>It's time for us to follow different paths.</i>

00:18:56.380 --> 00:18:59.110
<i>Go. Follow it far, far away.</i>

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:02.150
<i>It doesn't matter how many years it takes.</i>

00:19:02.150 --> 00:19:04.110
<i>Win. Beat Kakeru.</i>

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:07.920
<i>Become a stronger runner than him.</i>

00:19:07.920 --> 00:19:09.570
<i>I'll be rooting for you.</i>

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:16.220
<i>It's finally time for me to release
that precious part of my soul.</i>

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:21.570
<i>Kansei University first-year
and older twin brother, Jo Taro</i>

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:23.310
<i>is running with a light step.</i>

00:19:23.310 --> 00:19:27.140
<i>He's re-passed Tokyo Academy,
and even passed Shinsei.</i>

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:34.150
<b>Shonan Bridge</b>

00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:33.170
<i>He has Jonan Bunka and
Nihonbashi Tech in his sights.</i>

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:37.320
<i>Two more. No...</i>

00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:42.140
<i>I'm pumped.</i>

00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:44.780
Jota!

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:49.410
Jota!

00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:51.370
<i>Hana?</i>

00:19:53.340 --> 00:19:54.790
<i>What's she doing here?</i>

00:19:55.150 --> 00:19:56.950
<i>Wasn't she watching
the starting line at Otemachi?</i>

00:19:56.950 --> 00:19:59.300
You can do it!

00:20:04.830 --> 00:20:06.140
<i>Could it be?</i>

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:07.510
<i>No, but—</i>

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:09.890
What?

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:11.850
What's he looking at?

00:20:13.300 --> 00:20:16.360
<i>Does she like me?</i>

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:21.380
<i>What? Seriously?!</i>

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:26.200
Bro!

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:32.400
Oh, wow!

00:20:32.400 --> 00:20:34.540
He's so strong during the actual event.

00:20:35.890 --> 00:20:38.630
<i>Kansei's showing a menacing final spurt.</i>

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:41.120
<i>With the explosive sprint
of a short-distance runner,</i>

00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:42.590
<i>he's climbed two ranks.</i>

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:44.760
Joji!

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:45.760
Hey!

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:48.520
Hana!

00:20:48.520 --> 00:20:49.260
Huh?

00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:51.770
I think...

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:55.730
...she likes me.

00:20:57.160 --> 00:20:59.900
Seriously?!

00:22:31.160 --> 00:22:32.330
Congratulations Takashi on
Running in the Hakone Ekiden

00:22:40.540 --> 00:22:42.560
Next time, “Even If I Break.”

00:22:40.540 --> 00:22:45.900
<b>Next time: Even If I Break</b>
